{
  "//": "Per-repo config for the shared malin-plugins hooks (C:/claude-plugins). Gate-class hooks FAIL CLOSED if this file is missing/malformed — see C:/claude-plugins/README.md for the schema.",
  "_claimLint": "2026-09-19: claim-lint BLOCKS in Butlery (Malin, plan 2026-09-18 decision 3); it ran in warn mode from 2026-09-02. It reports newly written prose that asserts something nothing measured — a universal quantifier, a number bound to a countable noun, an N-of-M, a file:line — when the same hunk carries no command deriving it. exemptPaths REPLACES the script's defaults rather than merging, so the inherited entries are restated here. The entries beyond them were each measured for their own effect before being added: two are dated decision records of the same class as an ADR, and adoption-status.md carries a generator banner in its own first lines saying to re-run the tool rather than hand-edit — a warning there would be unactionable by construction. Two files that LOOK exemptable are deliberately gated, on the advice of the session working here: ACCEPTED_LARGE_FILES.md and the Art. 30 retention registers record a MEASUREMENT of the code rather than a decision, and a measurement can rot — that session found stale numbers in both the day this was written. Nothing else suggested was added, because each removed no findings, and an exemption that removes nothing today is a blind spot tomorrow. tasks/todo.md is deliberately NOT exempt although it carries the largest share of findings: measured against each commit's parent, the great majority of those lines are newly written rather than old text moving down the file, and they are the kind this exists for — one names a source line number inside a plan document. Re-measure by driving hookMain with this config the way the hook does.",
